<!-- Status-bar notification icon.

     Android draws notification icons as a mask: it keeps the alpha channel and
     discards the colour, then tints the shape to match the system theme. A
     full-colour app logo would therefore render as a flat white square. This is
     a single-path, white-on-transparent glyph (a message bubble) sized to the
     24dp icon grid, referenced by
     `com.google.firebase.messaging.default_notification_icon` so both the OS
     (background/terminated push) and the foreground path draw the same icon. -->
